        "notes": "ProxyCreate validates object targets/handlers and routes get, set, has, deleteProperty, ownKeys, apply, construct, getPrototypeOf, and setPrototypeOf through handler traps when present. Absent traps fall back to the target/default runtime behavior, and the supported trap surface now enforces basic result-shape checks (for example ownKeys/getPrototypeOf/construct) plus callable/constructible target gating for apply/construct. Full Proxy invariant enforcement and descriptor-heavy traps remain unimplemented."
      },
